  "id": "Compound::DB00764 - Disease::DOID:3310",
  "verbalization": "Mometasone, a corticosteroid, is closely related to Flumethasone Pivalate and Methylprednisolone through a shared structural and pharmacological profile. These compounds all belong to the class of therapeutic corticosteroids, which are known for their anti-inflammatory and immunosuppressive effects. The evidence suggests that Mometasone may exert a similar mechanism of action as these related drugs, potentially by modulating inflammatory pathways. The observed relationships imply that Mometasone could be repurposed for the treatment of Atopic Dermatitis, as it shares a common therapeutic class with Methylprednisolone, which is already established as effective for this condition. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of structural and functional similarity in drug repurposing, where the shared biological context of corticosteroids may underpin their therapeutic efficacy.",
